[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2176","id":4849767008,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT-9fds8AAAABIRGSYA","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2176","diff_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2176.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2176.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2176","number":2176,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(R9-ROW-STALE): the automerge guard reads the rewrite the beat plans","user":{"login":"hpo-author[bot]","id":331381602,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOE8B7Yg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/hpo-author","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The record beat plans `**open**` → `**merged**` status rewrites (R9-ROW-STALE, already on main), but `automerge_refusals` refused every file whose status was not `added` — so a beat carrying rewrites could never automerge, and because the hold in `tests.yml`'s record job engages only on a guard pass, every push to main rebuilt and force-pushed `record/autofix` (25 rebuilds, one dismissed approver review), moving the head under any reviewer. The open beat, PR #2151, still stands on exactly 12 such rewrites plus 10 new rows. Secondary: `tests/delivery_status.py` counted those 12 stale rows as rowed, so the reporter stayed green over the stall.\n\nThe fix, in the guard's own philosophy (regenerate from API truth, never parse):\n\n- `modified_lines` — the `(deleted, added)` pair of a one-line rewrite's patch, or None: one `-`, one `+`, no context, no second change.\n- `_rewrite_refusal` — the deleted line must be a row of that number whose status run is the generator's own `**open**` (`line_status`, the same parser the write side's `_rewrite_granted` grants with; deliberately NOT regenerated, because an open row's title is often one the API no longer reports — #2159's is), and the added line is judged by the existing `_row_refusal`: byte-equal to what `row_line` builds from the API's live facts, `.` or the roster-group tail allowed. The record pull request's own row is never rewritten. Every other modified file is refused as before.\n- `tests/delivery_status.py`: `open_anchored` reads the `**open**` status run on a line `anchored` already accepted, and `classify` counts a merge carrying a sha as NOT rowed by such a row — the same class `row_matches_merge` plans the rewrite for, now visible to the reporter.\n\nWorkflow interaction, verified not assumed: `tests.yml`'s hold path needs NO change — it runs `--automerge-check --hold`, which reads `/pulls/{n}/files` generically and passes modified files into `automerge_refusals`; with the guard passing, the hold engages (`status: held`, no rebuild) and the existing approve-and-merge predicate runs over the same head.\n\nConsequence to expect: once this lands, `delivery-status` on main reports the 12 stale rows pending/overdue (measured live, below) until the beat carrying the rewrites merges; that reddening is the fix working, and the unblocked beat is what clears it. #2169 has no row and is among the beat's planned rows.\n\n## Head\n\nc02f7de88ba4de7f0d027b8b4defe34c6eff4c59 (branch `fix/record-rewrite-guard`, one commit on origin/main 664a4c05e3ead3100e252d3f2f2a0b4cdd230e00)\n\n## Mutation proof\n\n`python3 tools/audit/seat/record_row.py --self-test` under each sabotage, restored after each:\n\n- Added-line comparison dropped (`_rewrite_refusal` returns \"\" after the open-check): `2 self-test check(s) failed: automerge refuses: a rewrite whose added line is not the API's facts, automerge refuses: a rewrite whose added line still reads open`.\n- Deleted-line check dropped (`_rewrite_refusal`'s open-row arm deleted): `3 self-test check(s) failed: automerge refuses: edits a row, automerge refuses: a rewrite that deletes a merged row, not an open one, automerge refuses: a rewrite that deletes another number's row`.\n\n## Null control\n\n- Failing test FIRST: on the unmodified tree, `python3 tools/audit/seat/record_row.py --self-test` printed `3 self-test check(s) failed: classify: a merge whose row still reads open is not rowed, automerge: a generated open->merged rewrite passes, automerge: a rewrite with the roster suffix passes`.\n- Live, against the real PR #2151: origin/main's guard refused on all 12 rewrite files (`not a new file adding exactly one line (status modified, -1)`, exit 1); this branch's guard passes the same head (exit 0), so the hold engages with no force-push rebuild.\n- Live reporter over current main: unfixed `classify` reported `49 rowed, 8 pending, 1 overdue`; fixed reports `37 rowed, 12 pending, 9 overdue` — the 12 stale rows leave \"rowed\".\n\n## Figures\n\n- `python3 tools/audit/seat/record_row.py --self-test` → `record_row self-test: all checks passed` (exit 0).\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` → `STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED`; 16 metrics measured (derived: `tests/structure_budgets.json`'s 17 keys less `recorded_at`), all at or under budget.\n- `GH_TOKEN=… python3 tools/audit/seat/record_row.py --automerge-check --hold --repo tvofi/heatpump_optimizer --pr 2151` → `AUTOMERGE OK #2151 at (live head)`, exit 0 (read-only GETs).\n- `GH_TOKEN=… python3 tests/delivery_status.py --check` at this head over live main → `DELIVERY STATUS OVERDUE — 37 rowed, 12 pending, 9 overdue (overdue at 12 commits)`.\n\n## Red checks\n\nnone — the branch carries origin/main plus one commit; no check went red on it (the pre-fix reds above were produced deliberately as the failing-test-first step, before the fix existed on the branch).\n\n`delivery-status` — red on main, and this diff touches what it reads: the red IS the defect this pull request fixes. The stale-row debt (12 merged pull requests whose rows still read `**open**`) that the fixed classify() now counts as unrowed turns the reporter red until the rewrite beats land; the cheaper detector is the reporter itself, and its standing cost is one non-required check on main until the beat clears the rows.\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone — the RCA (`automerge_refusals` vs the rewrite beat) was established by the root-cause seat; this PR is its fix. No later stage is constrained by anything found here.\n\n## Friction\n\nnone.\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T21:33:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T22:10:13Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T22:10:10Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T22:10:10Z","merge_commit_sha":"1cb2bedfae47ba4d2dcffe5566b0ff69fb594708","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2176/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2176/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2176/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/c02f7de88ba4de7f0d027b8b4defe34c6eff4c59","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/record-rewrite-guard","ref":"f